This is a smoke test to test the i2c-dev kernel module

Description: Loads i2c-dev module, then checks if there is any i2c devices activate on the board.
If buses are activated it will show it's name and the address.

Test inputs:
TmpDir=$(mktemp -d)
touch $TmpDir/list.txt $TmpDir/adapter_info.txt

Expected results:
:: [ 11:00:10 ] :: [   PASS   ] :: Command 'ls /sys/class/i2c-adapter/ > /tmp/tmp.XaJBStiFYM/list.txt 2>/dev/null' (Expected 0, got 0)
:: [ 11:00:10 ] :: [   LOG    ] :: I2C adapters found, reading information.
:: [ 11:00:10 ] :: [   PASS   ] :: Reading bus name (Expected 0, got 0)
:: [ 11:00:10 ] :: [   PASS   ] :: Reading bus address (Expected 0, got 0)
:: [ 11:00:10 ] :: [   PASS   ] :: Reading bus name (Expected 0, got 0)
:: [ 11:00:10 ] :: [   PASS   ] :: Reading bus address (Expected 0, got 0)
:: [ 11:00:11 ] :: [   LOG    ] :: Bus names and address.
:: [ 11:00:11 ] :: [   PASS   ] :: Command 'cat /tmp/tmp.XaJBStiFYM/adapter_info.txt' (Expected 0, got 0)

Results location:
output.txt

